From: Sander van Deijck <sander@vandeijck.com>
Subject: mbedtls: port the crypto and TLS backend to Mbed TLS 4.x

Port src/crypto/crypto_mbedtls.c and src/crypto/tls_mbedtls.c (added by
patches 110-135) to Mbed TLS 4.1 / TF-PSA-Crypto 1.1.

Most of the work is 39 commits from the Zephyr project's fork of this
backend (zephyrproject-rtos/hostap, crypto_mbedtls_alt.c and
tls_mbedtls_alt.c), which descends from the same Glenn Strauss code.
Those moved hashes, HMAC, PBKDF2, HKDF, key wrap, ECDH, ECDSA keys, PK
and the RNG to PSA. OpenWrt-specific changes on top:

- drop the pre-4.x version branches;
- PSA helpers the Zephyr changes call (they live outside hostap there);
- the AES block API on PSA;
- finite-field DH (WPS group 5, EKE, IKEv2) on the private bignum
  interface, since 4.x has neither DHM nor non-RFC 7919 FFDH groups.
  Zephyr instead compiles dhm.c back into its own TF-PSA-Crypto, which a
  shared libtfpsacrypto package cannot do;
- FIPS 186-2 PRF from hostap's internal SHA-1; guard secp192r1/secp224r1;
- TLS group names via MBEDTLS_SSL_IANA_TLS_GROUPS_INFO; skip the EAP-FAST
  suites 4.x removed.

The SAE/EAP-pwd/DPP point and bignum arithmetic, which PSA does not
offer, still uses mbedtls/private/{bignum,ecp,ecdsa,cipher}.h under
MBEDTLS_DECLARE_PRIVATE_IDENTIFIERS, as Zephyr does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

